//! English explanations of System › Packages (G1.6b), scope `packages`, sorted by key.

/// Explanations: (key, Markdown).
pub(super) const HELP: &[(&str, &str)] = &[
    ("menu.packages", "## What it does\nThe router's system image, in two slots (A/B): which one runs, the version and kernel of each, signature and dm-verity, and the update — install into the other slot, reboot on trial, confirm or come back by itself."),
    ("packages.boot", "## Boot\n\n**default**: the slot the firmware boots (first in `BootOrder`). **next boot**: the slot the next reboot tries once (`BootNext`, a trial). The `Boot####` entry carries the slot's kernel command line (hover it): the dm-verity table, the Tuning › Boot parameters, `corerouter.slot`."),
    ("packages.channel", "## Channel\n\nWhere the image comes from, RouterOS names: **stable**, **long-term**, **testing**, **development** (a local build). Informational: any package signed by a trusted key installs."),
    ("packages.confirm", "## Confirm\n\n**auto**: the new slot confirms itself once the daemon has been up for 10 s and every interface that had an address and was running before the update runs again (management reachable). **manual**: an operator must press Confirm (or run `system.package.confirm`) within the timeout, like Junos `commit confirmed` — use it when only a person can tell that the box works."),
    ("packages.downgrade", "## Downgrade\n\nWithout a package file: boots the other slot, which must hold an **older** image, on trial (RouterOS `/system package downgrade`). With a file: installs that older package into the other slot.\n\nThe configuration goes back too: the snapshot taken when that slot was left, when the older image reads its format."),
    ("packages.kernel", "## Kernel\n\nThe Linux version inside the slot's image (the kernel is part of the image: it is updated with it)."),
    ("packages.overview", "## Packages (A/B image)\n\nThe router keeps two complete images. An update is written to the slot that is **not** running, checked (signature, SHA-256 of each part, dm-verity tree read back from the disk), and booted **once on trial** through the UEFI `BootNext`. Confirmed, it becomes the default; not confirmed in time (or not booting at all), the next boot is the previous slot again, by itself, with the configuration it had.\n\nThe running slot is never written. A package has to be signed (Ed25519) by a key the image trusts.\n\nOutside the CoreRouter image (a PC with `--backend linux`, a browser) this is off and says why."),
    ("packages.path", "## Package file\n\nA `.crpkg` on the router: a file (`/tmp`, `/config`) or a block device holding one (a USB stick). **Check** reads it and verifies its signature and hashes without writing anything; **Install and reboot** writes it to the other slot."),
    ("packages.scrub", "## Scrub\n\nReads the standby slot from the disk and recomputes its dm-verity tree against the signed root hash: is it still a good fallback? Takes a fraction of a second for today's image."),
    ("packages.slot", "## Slot\n\nOne of the two root partitions (`rootfs-a`, `rootfs-b`), each with its kernel on the ESP. **this boot** marks the running one."),
    ("packages.snapshot", "## Configuration snapshots\n\nBefore a slot change, the whole `/config` (with its `format_version`) is copied to `package/config-<slot>`. A trial that fails comes back with it; a downgrade boots the configuration that slot last ran."),
    ("packages.state", "## State\n\n**running**: this boot. **standby**: a good image, the fallback. **trial**: armed or booted on trial, not confirmed. **failed**: its last trial did not confirm (hover: why). **invalid**: its header does not verify. **empty**: no image."),
    ("packages.timeout", "## Timeout\n\nSeconds the trial boot has to confirm (30 to 3600; default 300). Counted from the start of the trial boot; past it, init reboots and the firmware boots the previous slot."),
    ("packages.trial", "## Trial boot\n\nThe new slot boots once (UEFI `BootNext`, deleted by the firmware as it boots it). Every failure — kernel panic, a parameter that does not boot, a daemon that never answers, a power cut — ends in the previous slot, because it is still first in `BootOrder`. **Cancel** drops an armed trial before the reboot."),
    ("packages.verified", "## Verified\n\n**signed**: the slot's header is signed by a key the image trusts (key id in the tooltip). **dm-verity**: the running root is checked block by block against the signed root hash as it is read (a changed block fails the read). **no verity**: booted by the fallback path (the kernel's built-in command line), as the very first boot of a written image does."),
    ("packages.version", "## Version\n\nThe image's version; the tooltip has the commit and the build number that orders versions (an update cannot go below the running one: use Downgrade)."),
];
